      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If/when VRchats servers can scan uploaded avatars and somehow scan worlds containing avatars and give higher visibility to avatar worlds containing good ranked avatars.\nI imagine world discoverability will be redone at some point, so this could tie into that? Avatar worlds with piss poor avatars gets put further back in the list and properly optimized ones gets put first?\nOr maybe even quickly flash the performance rank on the UI for a second or two when changing into an avatar, so the user immediately is aware how awful or good it actually is.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-24T10:42:14.982Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be very useful, to get a new tab in worlds menu, called \"featured Avatar Worlds\" or feature them in the spotlight tab, If those avatars available in those worlds, are performance optimized. This would give content creators, a big reason, to care about avatar performance, before making them available for the community! Me and my friends, visited mostly all new popular avatar worlds, since over a year and there are so many fps eating Avatars out there with 300k+ Polys and terrible particles. Even for Quest... And still today, we see those Avatars, get popular really quick, If they look good. Destroying the VRC experience for other Players. It's terrible to see good looking avatars, which could easily be scaled down to 70k Polygons or less, but are lagging everyone out, cause of unoptimization!\nWe all know, an argument against this would be \"just hide them!\", but If we are honest to our self, for a single second... Who wanna play a game, that is either low fps or filled with grey robots???\nRight. No one!\nPushing optimized content, is the best way, to improve VRChat's performance long-term, without the need of adding any more limits or restrictions, when it comes to uploading avatar worlds!",
